<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Malaspina</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Malaspina family</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Malaspina were a feudal family of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lunigiana">Lunigiana</a> in north-western Tuscany, descended from the Obertenghi. Divided into many branches, they held castles in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apennines">Apennines</a>, lands in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> from the 13th century and later the lordship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/massa-tuscany">Massa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carrara">Carrara</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dante-alighieri">Dante</a> praised their hospitality in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/purgatorio">Purgatorio</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/malaspina.jpg" alt="Malaspina" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: FootKalos1597 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_the_House_of_Malaspina_(Spino_Fiorito)_(2).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
